<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Holy Priest Healer in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Holy Priest Healer Phase 4</h2>
<i>Healer gearing always heavily depends on playstyle, situation and raid environment so treat the BiS list below as a guideline rather than a gospel.</i>
<br/>
<br/>As the new T10 four set boosts your <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=34866/circle-of-healing">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_circleofrenewal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Circle of Healing</span></a> by a massive 10% while also granting you decent stats from the tier items themselves, you are able to completely shed your old offset once you get enough emblems to purchase four pieces of ilvl 251 T10. <br/>
<br/>As you can farm enough emblems for the set in just three to four resets, your gearing path in this phase is fairly simple and will always involve holding out for the T10 4p and swapping it on all at once, or even one-by-one if they are more powerful than your old pieces. <br/>
<br/>Finally, while the set below is primarily gemmed for additional haste, <span style="color: yellow;">Holy</span> can make good use of most caster stats, so there are several viable ways to gem. Spell power gems in particular are definitely also a good choice. While your casts will be a bit slower overall, you gain extra healing on cooldown-based abilities like CoH and PoM and they're better for <span style="color: black;">Shadow</span> if you dualspec often.<br/>
